			 2025 Project Awards Special Legislation establishing the Tourism Revenue Preservation Fund requires that between 20 and 40 percent of annual appropriations be dedicated to public improvements.  With approximately $215,000 available for this purpose as of July 1, the CEDC reached out to Town Departments to solicit requests for funding.  CEDC received eleven (11) requests totaling approximately $209,720. Requests were reviewed and applicants attended a CEDC meeting to further discuss their applications and to answer committee questions.  Prioritizing awards to projects with connections to long-term planning efforts/goals and other leveraged funding, the Committee made ten (10)  awards totaling $157,720.  Funded projects include: •	$50,000 towards the construction of the Station Avenue School Playground •	$3,000 for Conservation area interpretive signs •	$12,000 for a Broadband grant match •	$20,000 for beautification of the Senior Center •	$37,720 for Chase Brook Park •	$15,000 for Revolutionary War grave markers •	$17,000 for Historic area interpretive signs •	$25,000 for the design of the Revolutionary War Monument •	$50,000 towards the construction of the Revolutionary War Monument 
		 
	 
 

 
